@startuml class-diagram
' Virtual Meeting Sentinel — domain model and the services that own it.
'
' Scope: the AGM core. The video module is a large subsystem in its own right and is shown
' collapsed here; expanding it would double the size of this diagram and halve its usefulness.
' See VIDEO_LIBRARY.md for that side.
'
' Render:  plantuml docs/diagrams/class-diagram.puml
'   or paste into https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml

title Virtual Meeting Sentinel — class diagram (AGM core)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FDFDFD
  BorderColor #7C86A0
  ArrowColor #4A5568
}
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #F7F8FA
  BorderColor #C3CAD6
}
hide empty members

package "Identity" {
  class AppUser {
    UUID id
    String username
    String email
    String phone
    String passwordHash
    --
    String role
    Set<String> extraRoles
    --
    String pinHash
    String totpSecret
    boolean totpEnabled
    Instant createdAt
  }
  note right of AppUser
    **role** is the primary role — exactly one of
    ADMIN / MODERATOR / SHAREHOLDER / ATTENDEE.
    **extraRoles** are duties granted on top
    (MEETING_MANAGER, USER_MANAGER), any number,
    because they are orthogonal to being a
    moderator or a shareholder.

    passwordHash is nullable: an account created
    through Google has never had one.
  end note

  class WebAuthnCredential {
    UUID id
    String credentialId
    String publicKeyCose
    long signCount
  }
  AppUser "1" *-- "0..*" WebAuthnCredential : passkeys
}

package "The meeting" {
  class Meeting {
    UUID id
    String title
    String description
    Instant scheduledAt
    MeetingStatus status
    double quorumThresholdPercent
    Instant activatedAt
    Instant closedAt
  }
  note right of Meeting
    **At most one ACTIVE meeting**, enforced by a
    partial unique index rather than by application
    code — two moderators activating at once is a
    race the database can settle and the service
    cannot.

    Everything else scopes to whichever meeting is
    active: see MeetingScope.
  end note

  enum MeetingStatus {
    DRAFT
    ACTIVE
    CLOSED
  }

  class MeetingMember {
    UUID id
    UUID meetingId
    String username
    String roleInMeeting
    int votingWeight
    String addedBy
  }
  note bottom of MeetingMember
    The register of who may vote and for how much.
    **votingWeight lives here, not on AppUser** — a
    holding is a fact about one meeting, and last
    year's shareholding is not this year's.
  end note

  Meeting "1" *-- "0..*" MeetingMember
  Meeting -- MeetingStatus
  MeetingMember "0..*" -- "1" AppUser : username
}

package "Questions and topics" {
  class Question {
    UUID id
    String text
    String attendeeId
    float weight
    UUID clusterId
    UUID meetingId
    Instant createdAt
  }
  note right of Question
    **clusterId comes from the AI service**, which
    embeds the text and assigns it to the nearest
    centroid within the same meeting.

    meetingId is stamped unconditionally, whether or
    not the MEETINGS feature is on — partitioning
    that followed the flag would leave everything
    ingested with it off in the wrong partition the
    moment it was switched on.
  end note

  class ClusterDraft {
    UUID clusterId
    UUID meetingId
    String draftAnswer
    String citations
    boolean published
    String title
    String tags
  }

  class ClusterMerge {
    UUID fromClusterId
    UUID intoClusterId
  }
  note bottom of ClusterMerge
    A durable redirect. The AI service keeps centroids
    in memory and would happily recreate a cluster that
    was merged away, so the merge has to survive here
    rather than there. Followed with a cycle guard and
    a depth limit — see ClusterCurationService.
  end note

  class ClusterUpvote {
    UUID clusterId
    String voterId
  }

  Question "0..*" --> "0..1" ClusterDraft : clusterId
  ClusterDraft "1" -- "0..*" ClusterUpvote
  Meeting "1" *-- "0..*" Question
  Meeting "1" *-- "0..*" ClusterDraft
}

package "Voting" {
  class Resolution {
    UUID id
    UUID meetingId
    int seq
    String title
    String text
    ResolutionType type
    ResolutionStatus status
    boolean liveResultsVisible
    Instant openedAt
    Instant closedAt
  }

  enum ResolutionType {
    ORDINARY
    SPECIAL
    --
    carried(for, against)
  }
  note right of ResolutionType
    The majority rule lives on the enum, in integer
    arithmetic, so a percentage never rounds a vote
    the wrong way:
      ORDINARY : for > against
      SPECIAL  : for > 0 && for*4 >= (for+against)*3
    The positive guard is load-bearing — without it
    0 >= 0 reports an unvoted motion as carried.
  end note

  enum ResolutionStatus {
    DRAFT
    OPEN
    CLOSED
  }

  class Vote {
    UUID id
    UUID resolutionId
    UUID meetingId
    String username
    VoteChoice choice
    int weight
    Instant castAt
  }
  note bottom of Vote
    **weight is copied in at the moment of casting**,
    not read back from MeetingMember at tally time.
    A holding corrected mid-meeting must not silently
    restate votes already cast.

    One vote per member per resolution, enforced by a
    unique constraint.
  end note

  enum VoteChoice {
    FOR
    AGAINST
    ABSTAIN
  }

  Meeting "1" *-- "0..*" Resolution
  Resolution "1" *-- "0..*" Vote
  Resolution -- ResolutionType
  Resolution -- ResolutionStatus
  Vote -- VoteChoice
}

package "Access control" {
  class FeatureFlag {
    String key
    boolean enabled
    Set<String> allowedRoles
    String updatedBy
  }
  note right of FeatureFlag
    Stored config **overrides** the catalogue defaults
    in Feature.java. Tightening a default therefore
    does not tighten a running deployment — the row
    has to be changed too.
  end note
}

package "Video library" <<Rectangle>> {
  class "Video, VideoAsset, VideoRendition,\nVideoSegment, VideoComment, VideoLike" as VideoModule
}
Meeting ..> VideoModule : recordings\n(see VIDEO_LIBRARY.md)

' ---------------------------------------------------------------- services
package "Services" {
  class MeetingScope {
    Optional<UUID> activeMeetingId()
    Optional<UUID> knowledgeMeetingId()
  }
  note right of MeetingScope
    The single answer to "which meeting am I in?".
    activeMeetingId() respects the MEETINGS flag;
    knowledgeMeetingId() deliberately does not, so a
    per-document choice is honoured even with the
    flag off.
  end note

  class VotingService
  class ClusterCurationService
  class MeetingReportService
  class AuthService
  class FeatureService
  class AiClient
}

VotingService --> Resolution
VotingService --> Vote
VotingService --> MeetingMember : entitlement + weight
ClusterCurationService --> ClusterDraft
ClusterCurationService --> ClusterMerge
MeetingReportService --> Meeting
MeetingReportService --> Question
MeetingReportService --> Resolution
AuthService --> AppUser
FeatureService --> FeatureFlag
MeetingScope --> Meeting

class "AI service (FastAPI)" as AiService <<external>>
AiClient --> AiService : embed, cluster,\nRAG draft, search
note bottom of AiClient
  Every call goes through await(), which turns an
  unreachable service into a 503 with a readable
  message. A WebClientResponseException is passed
  through untouched — the service answered, and its
  reason is worth showing.
end note

@enduml
